```
$ lingrep-web --help
Web interface for lingrep pattern matching

Usage: lingrep-web [OPTIONS] --dict-path <DICT_PATH>

Options:
  -d, --dict-path <DICT_PATH>
          Path to the Vibrato dictionary (.dic.zst or .dic)
          
          [env: LINGREP_DICTIONARY_PATH]

  -i, --input <INPUT>
          Corpus input path; stdin is unsupported. Omit only when using --corpus.

      --input-format <INPUT_FORMAT>
          Override the inferred corpus format (commands may restrict accepted formats)
          
          [possible values: plain, jsonl, markdown, conllu, bccwj, soranoha, soranoha-tei, tei]

      --host <HOST>
          Address to bind. Loopback by default — change with `LINGREP_WEB_HOST` or `--host` to expose the service to other hosts (typically behind a reverse proxy that adds TLS and access control)
          
          [env: LINGREP_WEB_HOST]
          [default: 127.0.0.1]

  -p, --port <PORT>
          Port to listen on
          
          [env: LINGREP_WEB_PORT]
          [default: 3000]

      --base-path <BASE_PATH>
          Optional absolute path prefix used by a reverse proxy mount. Browser links remain relative, so a proxy can also rewrite its own root to this internal path
          
          [default: /]

      --max-kwic-lines-per-pattern <MAX_KWIC_LINES_PER_PATTERN>
          Maximum KWIC lines retained for each pattern
          
          [default: 1000]

      --max-active-sessions <MAX_ACTIVE_SESSIONS>
          Maximum number of concurrently retained workbench sessions
          
          [default: 256]

      --max-record-bytes <MAX_RECORD_BYTES>
          Maximum bytes accepted for one physical input record: a JSONL document, or a plaintext or Markdown line. A record larger than this stops the corpus build, reporting the record and its source
          
          [default: 1048576]

      --patterns <PATTERNS>
          lingrep patterns grammar file whose contents seed the pattern editor on the index page. Read once at startup; an unreadable file starts an empty editor
          
          [default: patterns/sentence-final.lx]

      --pattern-root <PATTERN_ROOT>
          Directory searched recursively for `*.lx` catalogs offered in the UI's catalog list. Defaults to the parent directory of `--patterns`, so the stock defaults discover `patterns/`. An unreadable directory yields an empty list rather than a startup failure

      --corpus <NAME=PATH>
          Additional corpus, as `NAME=PATH`. Repeatable. `NAME` is the URL key used by shareable links and must match `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}`; `default` is reserved for `--input`. All declared corpora share one dictionary and one reader configuration. `PATH` is a corpus source, or a prepared `.lingcorpus` artifact — read directly, and so unaffected by that shared reader configuration. Preparing an artifact with `ling corpus build` allows lingrep-web to serve formats without direct reader support, such as `bccwj`

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Markdown input:
      --md-include-sections <LIST>
          Include only lines carrying one of these section labels. By default, every label is included; an empty list is an error

      --md-exclude-sections <LIST>
          Exclude lines carrying one of these section labels. Pass "" to disable exclusions

      --md-self-labels <LIST>
          Treat these heading classes as labels for the heading line only, not for the section beneath it

      --md-recover-conversion-artifacts
          Recover conversion artifacts emitted by the corpus converter: presentational HTML, `<si ...>` notation, and div imbalance at physical document boundaries. `ling` rejects unrecovered artifacts unless this flag is passed; `lingrep-web` enables recovery unconditionally

```
